.TH ANIMA-ENGINE 1 "October 2026" "animaEngine" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
anima-engine \- animated characters that live on your desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B anima-engine
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B anima-engine
draws animated characters \(em pictures, GIFs, WebPs, short videos,
Shimeji packs, or the ten it draws itself \(em over the desktop, or
behind your windows. Clicks go through to the windows beneath. The
gear button in the top-right corner, or Ctrl+Shift+A, opens edit mode,
where they are added, arranged and changed; Escape leaves it.
.PP
A second start does not run a second copy: it brings up the one
running. It makes no network connection.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recover
Restore the crash-recovery snapshot over the live configuration (which
is first backed up to
.IR config.toml.bak ),
then exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANIMA_USE_WAYLAND_NATIVE=1
On a Wayland compositor with layer shell (KDE Plasma 6, sway, Hyprland,
river), draw through it rather than XWayland.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG=anima_engine=debug
More detailed logs on standard error.
.TP
.B ANIMA_NO_CACHE=1
Neither read nor write the decoded-frame cache.
.TP
.B __NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1
On a laptop with an NVIDIA GPU, draw on it; otherwise it is left asleep.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/animaengine/config.toml
Settings and the characters on screen.
.TP
.I ~/.config/animaengine/scenes/
Saved scenes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/animaengine/
The picture library, and the built-in characters' pictures.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/animaengine/
Decoded frames and thumbnails; safe to delete.
.SH SEE ALSO
The README, in
.IR /usr/share/doc/anima-engine/ ;
the FAQ and the full documentation at
https://github.com/Alexandru2984/animaEngine.
